    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d101">

                <pb facs="0214" n="114" sameAs="frus:frus1880/pg114"/>

                <head>No. 101.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Logan to Mr. Evarts.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States in Central America</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                rendition="#italic">Guatemala</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1879-12-20"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >December</hi> 20, 1879</date>. (Received January 22,
                        1880.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 45.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Under cover of this dispatch I inclose a
                    printed copy of the new constitution of Guatemala referred to in my dispatch No.
                    44. The articles discussed in that dispatch, numbered 5, 14, and 23, stand as
                    previously reported. I also inclose a copy of the note addressed by myself to
                    the minister of foreign relations in connection therewith.</p>
                <p>A note, in similar terms, was also addressed to the minister by the
                    representatives of Germany, France, Italy, Great Britain, and Spain. I also add
                    a translated copy of the minister’s reply. I shall be glad to receive any
                    instructions you may desire to give me.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>C. A. LOGAN.</signed></closer>




                <xi:include href="d101-a1.xml" xpointer="d101-a1"/>
                <xi:include href="d101-a2.xml" xpointer="d101-a2"/>
